From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jacob McSwain <jacob@mcswain.dev>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 04:53:51 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(gateway): a restart's listener relays to the standby
 that takes over

gateway.restart_listener_relay_seconds (0 = off): with restart_listener_handover, the listener stays open that many seconds after the profile is released and relays each connection to the address the standby published in gateway.standby, retrying until the successor listens. A successor in another network namespace (the next pod of a rolling update) then gets the clients instead of them being refused while it boots.
