+When the next gateway runs in another network namespace on the same home (the
+next pod of a rolling update on a shared volume), it opens its listener only
+after it took over, and a load balancer moves to it only once its readiness
+probe passed. Set `gateway.restart_listener_relay_seconds` (for example `15`)
+together with `gateway.restart_listener_handover` to keep the old listener open
+that long after the release instead: it relays every connection to the address
+the standby published in `gateway.standby` (its host name's address for a
+wildcard `webapp.host`), retrying until the next gateway listens, so clients
+wait instead of being refused. Allow connections between the two instances on
+the listener's port.
